{
    "_comment": [
        "A stand-in for a real system's published schema.json, so this repository can run",
        "`content-build content-format schema` in its own CI. package-build ships no system,",
        "so there is no real artifact here to point the check at.",
        "",
        "It is SoHL's own published schema.json at 0.8.2, plus exactly the fields the",
        "specification names that SoHL does not declare yet. Those three gaps are already",
        "tracked, so pointing CI at the real artifact would fail this repository's build for",
        "a reason that is not this repository's:",
        "",
        "  - HeroicLands/package-build#266 and Song-of-Heroic-Lands-FoundryVTT#1836 \u2014 the",
        "    in flags.sohl.docArchetype today and moves into the schema. The specification",
        "    template-priority field. The name is settled as `templatePriority` on all three",
        "    sides; SoHL still declares `system.archetype` until #1836 lands, so the fixture",
        "    takes the settled name and the check stays green on what is committed here.",
        "  - Song-of-Heroic-Lands-FoundryVTT#1781 \u2014 AffiliationDataModel gains `parents`,",
        "    `seat` and `domain`, and `relation` is renamed `relations`. The fixture adds all",
        "    four and keeps `relation`, since the artifact it was copied from still has it.",
        "  - Song-of-Heroic-Lands-FoundryVTT#1782 \u2014 `outcomeTrauma` is renamed",
        "    `outcomeTraumas`.",
        "",
        "So the delta above is the whole of the disagreement between the specification and a",
        "real published schema, and every other claim in the document is confirmed against a",
        "field SoHL genuinely declares. As those three land, this fixture is replaced by a",
        "fresh copy of the artifact and the delta goes to zero.",
        "",
        "Adding a `system.*` target to docs/content-format.md without adding it here fails",
        "CI, which is the point: the fixture is committed so the claim and the schema that",
        "receives it move together."
    ],
